'' RUN: 'select case true' matches the first true case (by-example BUG-flow-1). The literal
'' TRUE lowers as i8 -1, and the subject slot kept those bits while every case value is
'' coerced to the boolean subject, giving 1: no case matched, 'case true' included. The
'' subject is now stored normalised. A boolean variable subject and 'select case false'
'' were right already. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/select-case-true.bas -o tests/codegen/selectcasetrue.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/selectcasetrue.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: take a coat
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: lit ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: const ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: is ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: false ok
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: var ok
